VM-side adoption of php-runtime 8e9e810 (serialize.rs unserialize options / enum hook). Apply from the repo root with: git apply crates/php-runtime/proposals/vm-unserialize.diff
- context.rs: RuntimeContext::unserialize_enum_case for the VM, so E: values parsed by php-runtime (session, SPL legacy formats) fail with php-src's warnings/offsets instead of an Error exception.
- builtins/serial.rs: pub Vm::unserialize_options_in_effect(): the active unserialize() call's allowed_classes/max_depth/cur_depth (or the unserialize_max_depth ini outside one), with the docref function name; used by spl-unserialize.diff and session-unserialize.diff.
- errors.rs: docref_function_name() factored out of docref_bytes() (no behaviour change).
- iter.rs: foreach over $this from a parent's method lists the parent's private properties (visible_props recorded no declaring class, so op_fe_fetch's has_property_raw looked the name up in the child class and skipped it); fixes pdo_fetch_class_with_serialize_flag.

